<title>USA: U.N. approves 43rd Iraq oil sale for 900,000 bbls.</title>
<headline>U.N. approves 43rd Iraq oil sale for 900,000 bbls.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.N. overseers have approved the 43rd oil contract for Iraq under the oil-for-food accord, okaying the sale of some 900,000 barrels of oil, a U.N. spokesman said on Friday.</p>
<p>Terms of the latest sale call for an unspecified company to lift 10,000 barrels per day (bpd) of Iraqi crude over a 90-day period.</p>
<p>There were no new contracts pending at this time, the spokesman said.</p>
<p>Iraq is allowed to sell $2 billion worth of crude over a renewable six-month period, mainly to buy food and medicine for civilians suffering from sanctions slapped on Baghdad after it invaded Kuwait in August 1990.</p>
<p>The latest contract puts the total volume of oil sales at 115.09 million barrels.</p>
<p>((--Patrick Connole, NY Energy Desk, +1 212 859 1828))</p>
